{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments ["<b>And it shall come to pass, etc.</b> There are many who interpreted this of the hosts of the luminaries, but the correct interpretation is that they are angels who stand to help one nation and to be adversaries to another, and this is explained in the book of Daniel <small>(Daniel 10:13, etc.)</small>. Therefore he said, 'and upon the kings of the earth, upon the earth,' for the dominion of kings is bound up with the dominion of angels."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:55:01.739117890Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}